Abort a request when its client disconnects after it reached the scheduler.

Backport of upstream sglang f478b2bb2d, "Fix: abort handling for dispatched
requests after client disconnect" (sgl-project/sglang#35255, 2026-09-04), to
builds from before it (tested on 0.0.0.dev1+gd91c3682b, 2026-08-16, and on the
qwen4-main-squashed branch at 4ccff141db, 2026-09-07, which is the DGX Spark build).

Without it, a streaming client that disconnects mid-answer (Stop, a timeout, a
restart) has its request state deleted, so every later abort for it is ignored
and the scheduler keeps decoding it to max_tokens: a slot and its KV cache stay
taken by an answer nobody reads.

Apply with engine-patches/apply.sh. Not needed on sglang builds that include
the upstream fix; apply.sh detects that and skips.

Upstream-marker: sglang/srt/managers/tokenizer_manager.py abort_sent: bool

diff -ru a/sglang/srt/managers/scheduler.py b/sglang/srt/managers/scheduler.py
--- a/sglang/srt/managers/scheduler.py
+++ b/sglang/srt/managers/scheduler.py
@@ -2949,6 +2949,11 @@
             # it. Drop the marker once the request is actually gone.
             if req.finished() or req.req_pool_idx is None:
                 self._pending_chunked_abort_req = None
+                return
+            # The request moved to another scheduler queue after abort_request
+            # deferred it, so retry against its current location.
+            self._pending_chunked_abort_req = None
+            self.abort_request(AbortReq(rid=req.rid))
             return
 
         prepare_abort(req, "Aborted")
